Three errors:

1. `DenseMatrix::from_iterator` doesn't exist in smartcore 0.6.10 — arrowspace used it, but maybe under a different name or via trait import (`Array2::from_iterator`? or `DenseMatrix::from_iterator` requires `use smartcore::linalg::traits::svd...` no). Check smartcore DenseMatrix constructors: from_2d_vec (used in our common/mod.rs), from_iterator maybe on trait `Array2`? In smartcore there's `BaseMatrix`/`Array2` trait with `from_iterator`. Let me check what's available.

2/3. Closure move issues in compute_threshold_from_pilot's flat_map: closures capture counts/centroids by reference but I wrote `.filter(move |&j| counts[i]...)` and `.map(move |j| centroids[i]...)` — two separate `move` closures each trying to MOVE the vectors. Fix: don't use move; borrow instead. The flat_map structure needs i moved into inner closure. Rewrite as explicit nested loops:

```rust
let mut inter_dists: Vec<f64> = Vec::new();
for i in 0..k {
    for j in (i + 1)..k {
        if counts[i] > 0 && counts[j] > 0 {
            inter_dists.push(centroids[i].iter().zip(&centroids[j]).map(|(a,b)| (a-b)*(a-b)).sum());
        }
    }
}
```
Simpler and identical semantics/order (flat_map over i asc, j asc → same order).

For DenseMatrix construction: find the right constructor. Check smartcore 0.6.10 linalg basic matrix DenseMatrix methods + Array2 trait for from_iterator.

